{
  "schema": "mural.font-substitutions.v1",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "This catalog resolves font *names* that a source design (Refero clone, brand deck, screenshot) may request but that are NOT part of the redistributable OFL allowlist in font_bundle.FAMILY_FACES.",
    "Two kinds of entries: (1) aliases — the SAME family under a different spelling/variant name, resolved 1:1 to a canonical allowlist family; (2) mappings — a commercial or otherwise non-redistributable family, resolved to one or more portable candidate families that carry a similar voice.",
    "Commercial entries carry ONLY the requested name and metadata. They MUST NOT carry font file paths, download URLs, or binaries. Displaying a commercial name in a source design is not a redistribution license.",
    "Every mapping starts status:\"proposed\". Promotion to \"audited\" requires a visual specimen sign-off (rendered specimen under harnesses/mural-presenter-v1/canary/font-coverage/<run-id>/) confirming the substitute reads acceptably for the role. proposed mappings are NOT auto-enabled in production; the deterministic resolver will only emit resolution_kind audited_substitute for an audited mapping. A proposed mapping degrades to portable_fallback with the first candidate as the family, so the deck still renders and provenance is still recorded.",
    "Catalog invariants (enforced by font_bundle._validate_substitution_catalog): no alias cycles; an alias target must be a canonical allowlist family or another alias that ultimately resolves to one; a canonical allowlist family never appears as an alias source; an audited mapping's candidates must ALL exist in FAMILY_FACES; audited requires a non-empty specimen field. There is no silent swallow: a name with no alias and no mapping resolves to unmapped_fallback."
  ],
